@avlp/api:dev: {"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:41:57.198Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"37ae0d81-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\"schemaVersion\":\"one-shot-brief-v1\",\"subject\":\"Sleep and recovery physiology\",\"lessonTitle\":\"The Physiology of Rest: Mechanisms and Clinical Stakes\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":\"Rest as an active physiological process: memory consolidation, cardiovascular and metabolic recalibration, immune regulation, tissue repair, and downregulation of stress-axis activation during sleep and recovery\",\"sectionIds\":[\"d58cec4e-52be-75f6-bb84-d340d243ba6d\"]},{\"point\":\"Neurocognitive and affective costs of sleep loss: attention, working memory, decision-making and emotional control deficits, with meta-analytic evidence across 150+ studies showing reduced positive mood and increased anxiety\",\"sectionIds\":[\"6a3d9bac-cf28-72a4-b6b7-df55acfe035b\",\"5def3b58-c6f7-760d-9144-69cb1fa42c8e\"]},{\"point\":\"Cardiovascular strain mechanisms: sympathetic activation, inflammation, blood-pressure dysregulation and hormonal stress responses linking chronic short sleep to hypertension, coronary disease and stroke — with the key distinction that risk accrues over months and years, not single nights\",\"sectionIds\":[\"6682698e-7d9f-7b25-95e6-61cdd9846736\",\"2523c8ad-f165-727a-90ec-bf3fde906226\",\"20738034-c1fb-7eb3-8807-c331d4beff6c\"]},{\"point\":\"Metabolic consequences: reduced insulin sensitivity under sleep restriction, increased hunger and caloric intake, and the trajectory toward insulin resistance, metabolic syndrome and type 2 diabetes risk\",\"sectionIds\":[\"9255d18e-d24e-7eea-a032-a6a146cfebf5\",\"80de5b79-6501-7318-888b-0704158b7924\"]},{\"point\":\"Immune dysregulation: impaired immune signalling and elevated inflammatory markers (IL-6, C-reactive protein) after partial sleep deprivation in controlled studies\",\"sectionIds\":[\"dee3d032-2273-7202-a71a-7e3136fcb9b3\",\"aa6071d9-a312-7ac9-97eb-796fd6269b0c\"]},{\"point\":\"Bidirectional sleep–mental health relationship: disrupted sleep worsens emotional regulation, anxiety, depressive symptoms and stress tolerance, while psychiatric states disturb sleep\",\"sectionIds\":[\"3f9ee6a2","textChunks":["{\"schemaVersion\":\"one-shot-brief-v1\",\"subject\":\"Sleep and recovery physiology\",\"lessonTitle\":\"The Physiology of Rest: Mechanisms and Clinical Stakes\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":\"Rest as an active physiological process: memory consolidation, cardiovascular and metabolic recalibration, immune regulation, tissue repair, and downregulation of stress-axis activation during sleep and recovery\",\"sectionIds\":[\"d58cec4e-52be-75f6-bb84-d340d243ba6d\"]},{\"point\":\"Neurocognitive and affective costs of sleep loss: attention, working memory, decision-making and emotional control deficits, with meta-analytic evidence across 150+ studies showing reduced positive mood and increased anxiety\",\"sectionIds\":[\"6a3d9bac-cf28-72a4-b6b7-df55acfe035b\",\"5def3b58-c6f7-760d-9144-69cb1fa42c8e\"]},{\"point\":\"Cardiovascular strain mechanisms: sympathetic activation, inflammation, blood-pressure dysregulation and hormonal stress responses linking chronic short sleep to hypertension, coronary disease and stroke — with the key distinction that risk accrues over months and years, not single nights\",\"sectionIds\":[\"6682698e-7d9f-7b25-95e6-61cdd9846736\",\"2523c8ad-f165-727a-90ec-bf3fde906226\",\"20738034-c1fb-7eb3-8807-c331d4beff6c\"]},{\"point\":\"Metabolic consequences: reduced insulin sensitivity under sleep restriction, increased hunger and caloric intake, and the trajectory toward insulin resistance, metabolic syndrome and type 2 diabetes risk\",\"sectionIds\":[\"9255d18e-d24e-7eea-a032-a6a146cfebf5\",\"80de5b79-6501-7318-888b-0704158b7924\"]},{\"point\":\"Immune dysregulation: impaired immune signalling and elevated inflammatory markers (IL-6, C-reactive protein) after partial sleep deprivation in controlled studies\",\"sectionIds\":[\"dee3d032-2273-7202-a71a-7e3136fcb9b3\",\"aa6071d9-a312-7ac9-97eb-796fd6269b0c\"]},{\"point\":\"Bidirectional sleep–mental health relationship: disrupted sleep worsens emotional regulation, anxiety, depressive symptoms and stress tolerance, while psychiatric states disturb sleep\",\"sectionIds\":[\"3f9ee6a2","-c35e-740b-be75-c483078f3c78\"]},{\"point\":\"Recovery debt in training: the progression from functional fatigue to non-functional overreaching and overtraining syndrome when stress repeatedly exceeds recovery capacity\",\"sectionIds\":[\"424abc6f-db23-7579-909d-ea1374486355\",\"dffba253-7f88-7431-85e1-b68fd74dd618\"]},{\"point\":\"The stress → recovery → adaptation model as clinical bottom line: chronic underrecovery as the true risk, evidence-based sleep duration consensus (7+ hours), and why active recovery often beats complete inactivity\",\"sectionIds\":[\"98281838-f7a6-75cd-abd1-2d4e0abc8502\",\"a5eea29f-361a-77ac-b514-ada7faa52e86\",\"0a679116-48c1-7438-b525-b2254969517a\",\"1327df3d-e7b1-7a06-a932-627c26edecc8\"]}],\"notCovered\":[\"Occupational fatigue, errors and accident risk in driving, machinery and medical work (section 47694dee) — omitted to keep focus on physiological mechanisms rather than occupational safety\",\"The 'five hours instead of eight' productivity misconception section (30438e8b) — its content is implicitly addressed by the neurocognitive deficits coverage\",\"Micro-breaks, fatigue and vigour meta-analysis (1eb88c2e) — the outline provides only a citation link with no supporting text to build a scene on\",\"Benefits of adequate rest overview (2d2a472f) covered only as folded into the recovery-cycle framing, not as a standalone list\"],\"plannedSceneCount\":12,\"stylePackId\":\"systems\",\"stylePackReason\":\"Precise diagrams and fine connectors suit mechanism-driven content — stress axes, inflammatory pathways, dose-response risk — for a practitioner audience that wants cause and effect, not decoration.\",\"soundBed\":\"quiet-pulse\",\"soundBedReason\":\"A focused, calm pulse sustains clinical seriousness and momentum for dense mechanistic material without distracting from technical narration.\"}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":3803,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":21851,"service":"api","correlationId":"01a11850-8e35-73cc-a9b5-000a01137296"}}
