@avlp/pipeline-worker:dev: {"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:46:31.038Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"3adc9073-aws_ew1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"narration-v1\",\n  \"targetDurationSeconds\": 300,\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a11852-bf88-7b8a-bb21-2b2d3b596e04\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Rest is the most underrated intervention in clinical medicine.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Hook framing required by the outline; restates the lesson's thesis rather than a sourced factual claim.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"We treat it as downtime, as the absence of work, but physiologically it is anything but passive.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Rest is an active component of the body's recovery apparatus, engaging multiple organ systems at once.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Withhold it, and the consequences are measurable across neurocognitive performance, cardiometabolic trajectory, and psychiatric comorbidity.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9eec6c71-abc2-7bc6-91ca-cd15dc252fb4\", \"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\", \"6b86335a-0ad4-72b2-bb3f-d7433f3a0ea3\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"And the pathology does not accrue from a single bad night.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"It accrues from chronic underrecovery, sustained over months and years.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\", \"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a11852-bf88-7e45-a78c-422c79481e81\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"So what actually happens during adequate rest? Five distinct recovery mechanisms execute.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text","textChunks":["{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"narration-v1\",\n  \"targetDurationSeconds\": 300,\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a11852-bf88-7b8a-bb21-2b2d3b596e04\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Rest is the most underrated intervention in clinical medicine.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Hook framing required by the outline; restates the lesson's thesis rather than a sourced factual claim.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"We treat it as downtime, as the absence of work, but physiologically it is anything but passive.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Rest is an active component of the body's recovery apparatus, engaging multiple organ systems at once.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Withhold it, and the consequences are measurable across neurocognitive performance, cardiometabolic trajectory, and psychiatric comorbidity.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9eec6c71-abc2-7bc6-91ca-cd15dc252fb4\", \"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\", \"6b86335a-0ad4-72b2-bb3f-d7433f3a0ea3\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"And the pathology does not accrue from a single bad night.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"It accrues from chronic underrecovery, sustained over months and years.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\", \"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a11852-bf88-7e45-a78c-422c79481e81\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"So what actually happens during adequate rest? Five distinct recovery mechanisms execute.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text","\": \"First, the brain consolidates memory, stabilizing what was learned during waking hours.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Second, the cardiovascular and metabolic systems recalibrate, resetting regulatory set-points.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Third, immune activity is actively regulated rather than left unchecked.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Fourth, tissues repair the damage accumulated under physical stress.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Fifth, the nervous system downshifts, moving away from sustained stress activation.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"On the evidence hierarchy, sleep carries the strongest support, but work breaks and post-exercise recovery periods are also backed by data.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Conceptually, then, rest is an anabolic, regulatory window, a period of active physiological maintenance, not passive idleness.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a11852-bf88-7c7d-a9e9-a01f216d81ab\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Start with the brain, because this is where sleep loss bites first.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Transitional framing sentence for the section; ordering claim is a narration choice rather than a sourced fact.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The deficit profile is specific: attention narrows, reaction time slows, an","d working memory degrades.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9eec6c71-abc2-7bc6-91ca-cd15dc252fb4\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Learning, decision-making, and emotional control all deteriorate in parallel.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9eec6c71-abc2-7bc6-91ca-cd15dc252fb4\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Clinically, this presents as poor concentration, forgetfulness, irritability, impaired judgement, low motivation, and the cognitive fog patients so often describe.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9eec6c71-abc2-7bc6-91ca-cd15dc252fb4\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The affective dimension is equally robust.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9eec6c71-abc2-7bc6-91ca-cd15dc252fb4\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Experimental findings aggregated across more than one hundred and fifty studies show that sleep loss reliably suppresses positive mood while elevating anxiety symptoms.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9eec6c71-abc2-7bc6-91ca-cd15dc252fb4\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"That is not a soft association; it is a consistent experimental signal across a very large evidence base.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9eec6c71-abc2-7bc6-91ca-cd15dc252fb4\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a11852-bf88-7285-b9ee-c744dd77c106\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Now trace the cardiovascular chain, because the mechanism matters for how you counsel patients.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Transitional framing for the professional audience; signals clinical relevance without asserting a sourced fact.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Insufficient sleep engages the sympathetic nervous system, upregulates inflammation, disrupts blood-pressure regulation, and perturbs hormonal stress responses.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\"]\n        },\n        ","{\n          \"text\": \"These four pathways converge on a common endpoint.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Chronically short sleep is associated with hypertension, coronary heart disease, and stroke.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"But here is the distinction that should shape your risk framing.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Rhetorical signpost highlighting the clinical distinction the outline asks to stress; no new factual claim.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"One poor night does not cause heart disease.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The concern is repeated inadequate recovery compounding over months and years.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"That temporal framing lets you reassure the occasionally sleep-deprived patient while still intervening on the chronically underrecovered one.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a11852-bf88-7a71-836c-cda222a161ec\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The metabolic sequence unfolds stepwise, and each link has evidence behind it.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a1a47b52-c81d-796a-b306-839490391e8d\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Link one: sleep restriction reduces insulin sensitivity.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a1a47b52-c81d-796a-b306-839490391e8d\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Link two: under sleep deprivation, hunger rises and caloric intake increases.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a1a47b52-c81d-796a-b306-839490391e8d\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Note t","he evidentiary quality here, because it is unusually strong for lifestyle medicine.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Evaluative signpost preparing the randomized-trial point; the characterization of lifestyle medicine is narrator commentary, not a sourced claim.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The hunger and intake findings come from randomized trials, not merely observational correlation.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a1a47b52-c81d-796a-b306-839490391e8d\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"That elevates them above the usual diet-and-sleep epidemiology.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a1a47b52-c81d-796a-b306-839490391e8d\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Sustained over time, this physiology drives weight gain, insulin resistance, and metabolic syndrome.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a1a47b52-c81d-796a-b306-839490391e8d\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The terminal outcome is an elevated risk of type 2 diabetes.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a1a47b52-c81d-796a-b306-839490391e8d\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a11852-bf88-761e-beb5-bb24aad6c5fa\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The relationship between sleep and mental health is not one-directional; it is a loop.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"6b86335a-0ad4-72b2-bb3f-d7433f3a0ea3\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Anxiety and depression disturb sleep architecture from one side.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"6b86335a-0ad4-72b2-bb3f-d7433f3a0ea3\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"From the other, insufficient or disrupted sleep degrades emotional regulation.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"6b86335a-0ad4-72b2-bb3f-d7433f3a0ea3\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The documented consequences of sleep deficiency include increased anxiety, depressive symptoms, heightened emotional reactivity, poorer stress toleranc","e, and diminished positive emotion.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"6b86335a-0ad4-72b2-bb3f-d7433f3a0ea3\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The clinical implication is threefold, and worth stating explicitly.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Rhetorical signpost introducing the interpretive framing that follows; carries no sourced factual content.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Sleep disruption is simultaneously a symptom of psychiatric illness, a perpetuating factor that worsens it, and a therapeutic entry point.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"The source documents bidirectional influence and its consequences; framing this as symptom, perpetuating factor, and treatment target is a clinical interpretation offered to make the reciprocity actionable for practitioners.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Treating sleep is therefore never merely symptomatic management; it is an intervention on the loop itself.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Extends the preceding generated interpretation into a practice implication; the source supports bidirectionality but not this prescriptive framing.\"\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a11852-bf88-7584-9b5f-9f6d4609c9f7\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The body runs on a stress, recovery, adaptation cycle, and that model clarifies who is actually at risk.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Without adequate recovery, prolonged stress converts into physiological strain.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\":"," \"Acute fatigue, an occasional poor night or an exceptionally busy week, is unlikely to cause lasting harm in an otherwise healthy person.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Chronic underrecovery is a different entity entirely: persistently short sleep, work without meaningful breaks, intense training without recovery, or months of unrelenting psychological stress.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The evidence links that chronic state to poorer cognition, emotional problems, impaired metabolic health, increased inflammation, weakened immune regulation, cardiovascular disease, injury, and reduced physical performance.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Now the applied contrast. Recovery does not demand inactivity.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b874bce9-1d1f-70cb-8b51-1c9d1e7f9dd0\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Walking, moderate exercise, stretching, hobbies, and time outdoors can all support recovery, depending on what you are recovering from.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b874bce9-1d1f-70cb-8b51-1c9d1e7f9dd0\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The cognitively exhausted desk worker will likely benefit more from a walk than from lying in bed scrolling social media.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b874bce9-1d1f-70cb-8b51-1c9d1e7f9dd0\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"And one nuance: very long habitual sleep also associates with poorer outcomes, but likely as a marker of underlying illness rather than a cause.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b874bce9-1d1f-70cb-8b51-1c9d1e7f9dd0\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a11852-bf88-7833-81b0-28c513d7a7d8\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"So the synthesis. Rest executes five active recovery mechanisms, not none.\",\n          \"sourceBl","ockIds\": [\"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Sleep loss produces quantifiable neurocognitive and affective deficits, backed by more than one hundred and fifty experimental studies.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"9eec6c71-abc2-7bc6-91ca-cd15dc252fb4\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Cardiovascular and metabolic harms follow cumulative trajectories spanning months to years, not single nights.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0a0f0502-0564-77b7-8c06-23269be050cd\", \"a1a47b52-c81d-796a-b306-839490391e8d\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Sleep and mental health degrade one another bidirectionally.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"6b86335a-0ad4-72b2-bb3f-d7433f3a0ea3\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"And the stress, recovery, adaptation model names the true clinical target: chronic underrecovery, not isolated fatigue, with active recovery frequently outperforming inactivity.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\", \"b874bce9-1d1f-70cb-8b51-1c9d1e7f9dd0\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Rest, in short, is prescribable physiology.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Closing aphorism consolidating the lesson thesis; a rhetorical summary label rather than a sourced factual claim.\"\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":15430,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":55888,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a11850-8e35-73cc-a9b5-000a01137296"}}
