mechanism-icon\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Icon representing sustained short-sleep pattern as the convergent mechanism.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"effect-1-icon\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Icon for elevated blood pressure.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"effect-2-icon\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Icon for coronary artery pathology.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"effect-3-icon\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Icon for cerebrovascular events.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"template\": \"process\",\n      \"title\": \"Metabolic Progression: From Sleep Restriction to Type 2 Diabetes\",\n      \"narrationBlockIds\": [\n        \"01a11853-2f5a-7bf2-a5a1-6aa87da3bd5e\"\n      ],\n      \"onScreenText\": [\n        \"Hunger & intake: randomized-trial evidence, not just epidemiology.\"\n      ],\n      \"visual\": {\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"Sleep restriction\",\n          \"Reduced insulin sensitivity\",\n          \"Increased hunger & caloric intake (RCT)\",\n          \"Weight gain & insulin resistance\",\n          \"Metabolic syndrome\",\n          \"Elevated type 2 diabetes risk\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 39,\n      \"transition\": \"cut\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"a1a47b52-c","81d-796a-b306-839490391e8d\"\n      ],\n      \"generatedAdditions\": [],\n      \"assetRequirements\": [\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"step-1-icon\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Icon for sleep restriction as the initiating step.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"step-2-icon\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Icon for reduced insulin sensitivity.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"step-3-icon\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Icon for increased hunger and caloric intake.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"step-4-icon\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Icon for weight gain and insulin resistance.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"step-5-icon\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Icon for metabolic syndrome.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"step-6-icon\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Icon for elevated type 2 diabetes risk as terminal outcome.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"template\": \"labelled-diagram\",\n      \"title\": \"The Bidirectional Sleep–Mental Health Loop\",\n      \"narrationBlockIds\": [\n        \"01a11853-2f5a-76f0-a0a6-c6312cda3e81\"\n      ],\n      \"onScreenText\": [\n        \"Symptom, perpetuating factor, and therapeutic entry point.\"\n      ],\n      \"visual\": {\n        \"kind\": \"shapes\",\n        \"shape\": \"cycle\",\n        \"labels\": [\n          { \"text\": \"Anxiety & depression disturb sleep architecture\" },\n          { \"text\": \"Disrupted sleep degrades emotional regulation\" },\n          { \"text\": \"Greater reactivity; poorer stress tolerance\" },\n          { \"text\": \"Treating sleep intervenes on the loop\" }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 39,\n      \"transition\": \"fade\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"6b86335a-0ad4-72b2-bb3f-d7433f3a0ea3\"\n      ],\n      \"generatedAdditions\": [],\n      \"assetRequirements\": [\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"diagram\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Cycle diagram of the reciprocal sleep–mental-health loop with the four labelled nodes.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"template\": \"comparison\",\n      \"title\": \"Stress → Recovery → Adaptation, and Why Active Recov","ery Wins\",\n      \"narrationBlockIds\": [\n        \"01a11853-2f5a-7554-8ab4-a233876c51f7\"\n      ],\n      \"onScreenText\": [\n        \"Recovery ≠ inactivity; long sleep likely marks illness, not cause.\"\n      ],\n      \"visual\": {\n        \"leftSubject\": { \"label\": \"Acute fatigue\" },\n        \"rightSubject\": { \"label\": \"Chronic underrecovery\" },\n        \"similarities\": [\n          \"Both arise within the stress–recovery–adaptation cycle\"\n        ],\n        \"differences\": [\n          \"Occasional poor night vs months of short sleep\",\n          \"Unlikely lasting harm vs multi-system pathology\",\n          \"Resolves with rest vs cumulative strain\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 49,\n      \"transition\": \"slide\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\",\n        \"b874bce9-1d1f-70cb-8b51-1c9d1e7f9dd0\"\n      ],\n      \"generatedAdditions\": [],\n      \"assetRequirements\": [\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"left-subject-image\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Visual of acute, transient fatigue (single poor night or busy week).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"slot\": \"right-subject-image\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Visual of chronic underrecovery (persistently short sleep, no breaks, unrelenting stress).\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"template\": \"summary\",\n      \"title\": \"Clinical Synthesis: Rest as Prescribable Physiology\",\n      \"narrationBlockIds\": [\n        \"01a11853-2f5a-7c96-ab0c-6e0cd6cb0ac3\"\n      ],\n      \"onScreenText\": [],\n      \"visual\": {\n        \"takeaways\": [\n          { \"text\": \"Rest executes five active recovery mechanisms, not none.\" },\n          { \"text\": \"Sleep loss yields quantifiable neurocognitive and affective deficits (150+ studies).\" },\n          { \"text\": \"Cardiometabolic harms follow cumulative, months-to-years trajectories.\" },\n          { \"text\": \"Sleep and mental health degrade one another bidirectionally.\" }\n        ],\n        \"centralModel\": \"Target chronic underrecovery, not isolated fatigue — rest is prescribable physiol","ogy.\",\n        \"callToAction\": \"Prescribe recovery with the same rigor as any other intervention.\"\n      },\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 26,\n      \"transition\": \"fade\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\n        \"b168fb27-3f9e-791a-b576-c1319c55e426\",\n        \"0dd73264-3a04-721d-b42a-7a779096a67c\"\n      ],\n      \"generated